ve the sets $A$ and $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={0.5,2,\\sqrt{5}},\\,B={-1,0,1}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following mapping diagrams represents the following relation? \n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in A\\times B\\,:\\,{x}^{y}\\in Z}\n$$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 false] [17592186204249 1074 "The ordered pairs belonging to our relation correspond to the arrows on the mapping diagram. Each arrow starts at the first component of the pair and ends at its second component.\n\nWe're given the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{0.5,2,\\sqrt{5}\\},\\,B=\\{-1,0,1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$\n\n- If $x=0.5,$ then the values $y=-1,0$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(0.5,-1)$ and $(0.5,0),$ and we should add the arrows $0.5\\to -1$ and $0.5\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=0,1$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,0)$ and $(2,1),$ and we should add the arrows $2\\to 0$ and $2\\to 1$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=\\sqrt{5},$ then the value $y=0$ satisfies ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(\\sqrt{5},0),$ and we should add the arrow $\\sqrt{5}\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](images/d6/d66cabe448b2b33804721dd3cfa884de858a5e4fa6056991f612465070d54da5.png)" 13194139534477 17592186045417 true] [17592186204249 1074 "The ordered pairs belonging to our relation correspond to the arrows on the mapping diagram. Each arrow starts at the first component of the pair and ends at its second component.\n\nWe're given the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={0.5,2,\\sqrt{5}},\\,B={-1,0,1}.\n$$\n\nThe relation $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in A\\times B$ with ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$\n\n- If $x=0.5,$ then the values $y=-1,0$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(0.5,-1)$ and $(0.5,0),$ and we should add the arrows $0.5\\to -1$ and $0.5\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=2,$ then the values $y=0,1$ satisfy ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pairs $(2,0)$ and $(2,1),$ and we should add the arrows $2\\to 0$ and $2\\to 1$ to the mapping diagram.\n\n- If $x=\\sqrt{5},$ then the value $y=0$ satisfies ${x}^{y}\\in Z.$ So, $R$ contains the ordered pair $(\\sqrt{5},0),$ and we should add the arrow $\\sqrt{5}\\to 0$ to the mapping diagram.\n\nTherefore, we have the following plot:\n\n![](images/d6/d66cabe448b2b33804721dd3cfa884de858a5e4fa6056991f612465070d54da5.png)" 13194139534477 17592186045417 false] [17592186416062 1071 "Let $A=\\{1,2,3\\}.$ Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y=4\\}?$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 true] [17592186416062 1071 "Let $A={1,2,3}.$ Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R={(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}\\,:\\,x+y=4}?$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 false] [17592186416063 1071 "Let $A=\\{1,2,4\\}.$ Which of the following directed graphs represents the following relation? \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le {x}^{2}\\}\n$$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 true] [17592186416063 1071 "Let $A={1,2,4}.$ Which of the following directed graphs represents the following relation? \n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {A}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le {x}^{2}}\n$$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 false] [17592186416064 1071 "![](images/de/ded4e8a94730585809c5534fee8d401481c919d529a67cd088e96b8797f2b237.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set $\\{2,5,8\\}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(2,8)$\n\nIII. $(8,5)$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 true] [17592186416064 1071 "![](images/de/ded4e8a94730585809c5534fee8d401481c919d529a67cd088e96b8797f2b237.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set ${2,5,8}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(2,2)$\n\nII. $(2,8)$\n\nIII. $(8,5)$" 13194139534477 17592186045417 false] [17592186416065